 "notes": "Scalar UDM search via Cs optical spectroscopy (two apparatus). Headline single-coupling exclusion traced from Fig. 3 (vector file dmedirectionv.pdf), the solid red 'Exp. B, only d_me != 0' curve, which is the measured 95% C.L. bound (Exp. A is described as ultimate/projected sensitivity; Exp. B sets the actual limits, apply Eq.(5)). Galactic-halo scenario, rho_DM ~ 3e-6 eV^4 ~ 0.4 GeV/cm^3 (paper native density; not rescaled). The paper defines d_me = g_e * M_Pl^reduced / m_e,0 with reduced Planck mass M_Pl^reduced=2.4e18 GeV; the canonical convention uses kappa=sqrt(4pi)/M_Pl with M_Pl=1.22e19 GeV. Conversion d_me(canonical)=sqrt(2)*d_me(paper) applied to all points (factor sqrt(8pi/4pi)=sqrt(2)). The paper equally reports g_gamma (fine-structure coupling, Fig 2 bottom -> ScalarPhoton d_e); ScalarElectron/d_me chosen because Fig 3 presents it directly in the canonical variable. Curve spans m_phi ~ 2e-10 to 4e-7 eV (g_e bound applies for f>f_c1~50 kHz). The bump near ~5e-9 eV is a real feature of the plotted curve.",
